      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $B$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $6\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${B}^{T}$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $6\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
