    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $C$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $-6\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-6\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
